From c3762a4dc84d234efef451b2011cb1a0e163764b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] big-fella: no SCDC recheck while HPD is held low (i915)

linux-9913 looks at an HDMI sink's SCDC TMDS_Config after every hotplug, and
linux-9925 reports a short HPD drop as still connected. Together the recheck
ran while the LG G5 was dropping HPD after a Dolby Vision stop: the sink
wasn't answering, its TMDS_Config read as 0x00 (in the same millisecond as
"HPD low"), and intel_hdmi_reset_link made up to three modesets, 3.5-4 s of
black after every DV stop (petunia 2026-11-03: 28 drops, 47 "Sink's TMDS
config 0x00 doesn't match the link ... modeset", 21 "still wrong after 3
modesets").

intel_ddi_hotplug now skips intel_hdmi_reset_link while the connector's HPD
is held. HPD coming back is a new hotplug (hotplug_retries from 0), so
linux-9913's recheck looks at the sink for 4 s from then, which is when a
sink that came back with the wrong TMDS_Config (9913's case) is fixed.
Applies after linux-9925.

[Hades: taken as is from YBLOD 0.3.3 (dangerouslaser/libreelec-yblod
3b3a983f93, linux-9927-big-fella-hdmi-scdc-after-hold.patch, also in
big-fella e73aa82), as linux-9963. Their linux-9913 and linux-9925 are
linux-9959 and linux-9962 here. Upstream's intel_hdmi_reset_link() returned
early for a connector reported disconnected; the hold of linux-9962 keeps
it connected, so this skip is what keeps that case as it was.]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
index 46a6eef..533f022 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_ddi.c
@@ -4908,7 +4908,20 @@ intel_ddi_hotplug(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	state = intel_encoder_hotplug(encoder, connector);
 
 	if (!intel_tc_port_link_reset(dig_port)) {
-		if (connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA) {
+		/*
+		 * big-fella: not while HPD is held low (intel_hdmi_detect,
+		 * i915.hpd_hold_ms): the sink isn't answering then, and its SCDC
+		 * read as 0x00 forced up to three modesets, 3.5-4 s of black after
+		 * every Dolby Vision stop on an LG G5. HPD coming back is a new
+		 * hotplug (hotplug_retries from 0), so linux-9913's recheck still
+		 * looks at the sink for 4 s from then.
+		 */
+		if (connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA &&
+		    connector->hpd_held) {
+			drm_dbg_kms(encoder->base.dev,
+				    "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] HPD held low, SCDC not checked\n",
+				    connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name);
+		} else if (connector->base.connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA) {
 			intel_modeset_lock_ctx_retry(&ctx, NULL, 0, ret)
 				ret = intel_hdmi_reset_link(encoder, &ctx);
 			drm_WARN_ON(encoder->base.dev, ret);
